      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "A new route for the synthesis of functional aqueous nanogels decorated with a controlled amount of surface-drafted isoeugenol molecules has been developed. Obtained nanogels exhibit two key functions: a)\u2005antibacterial activity against different oral pathogens and b)\u2005cell-adhesive and -growth-promoting properties. Functional nanogels can be potentially used as building blocks in the design of bioactive coatings on various implants preventing infections and accelerating tissue regeneration."
      },
